    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0539" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg465"/>

                <head>Mr. Perry to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 140.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Madrid,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 9, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I hope to save the mail steamer by sending
                    direct to Queenstown, and thus to put in your hands a press copy of Mr. Consul
                    Dabney’s letter from Teneriffe of the 29th ultimo, received one hour since.</p>
                <p>Though the voyage of the steamer between Teneriffe and Cadiz has been unusually
                    long, perhaps the Calabar may not have reached Liverpool in time for Mr.
                    Dabney’s despatches for you to be put on board for New York.</p>
                <pb facs="0540" n="466" xml:id="pg466"/>
                <p>Nothing has been heard here of the new pirate vessel now undoubtedly under the
                    command of Semmes, who escaped from the wreck of the Alabama, since the transfer
                    of her armament and crew as related by Mr. Dabney.</p>
                <p>With great respect, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HORATIO J. PERRY,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d580-a1.xml" xpointer="d580-a1"/>
